VeridianOS: fix compiler warnings in Aurorae

GCC reported:

- -Wunused-result for QFile::open() in ConfigurationModule::initQml()
  (config/auroraeconfig.cpp). Real bug: if the theme's config.ui could not
  be opened, or opened but did not parse, QUiLoader::load() returned
  nullptr and the next line dereferenced it
  (customConfigForm->objectName()), crashing the configuration module.
  Both failures are now logged and return, as the function already does
  when the theme package, its metadata or the files are missing.
  (Prepared for upstream, invent.kde.org/plasma/aurorae.)
- -Wdeprecated-declarations for QHoverEvent::pos() and posF():
  - v1/aurorae.cpp, Decoration::hoverMoveEvent(): posF() -> position(),
    which posF() returned; unchanged.
  - v1/renderer.cpp, Renderer::forwardMouseEvent(): pos() -> position().toPoint(),
    which pos() returned; unchanged (the old position next to it is the
    integer oldPos() as well).
  - v2/decorationbuttongroup.cpp, DecorationButtonGroup::eventFilter():
    pos() -> position(); boundingRect() is a QRectF, so the hover test now
    uses the unrounded position instead of rounding it to whole pixels
    first.
- -Wdeprecated-declarations for QVariant::type() in
  Decoration::updateBlur() (v1/aurorae.cpp): compared through typeId(),
  which gives the same id for the built-in QRegion type; unchanged.

diff -ru a/config/auroraeconfig.cpp b/config/auroraeconfig.cpp
--- a/config/auroraeconfig.cpp
+++ b/config/auroraeconfig.cpp
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
